OL,3,GNEWSAOur baby died on Christmas Eve and
OL,4,Awe're still waiting for answers
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Brooke and Wil Rees-Webb took
OL,7,Ftheir newborn baby home in December
OL,8,F2025, they were expecting to enjoy
OL,9,Ftheir first Christmas together as a
OL,10,Ffamily.
OL,12,FBut Gwilym died on Christmas Eve at
OL,13,Fjust 11 days old. And, as the couple
OL,14,Ffrom Pontypridd, Rhondda Cynon Taf,
OL,15,Fprepare to mark his first birthday
OL,16,Fwithout him, they are still waiting for
OL,17,Fanswers about his unexplained death.
OL,19,FBaby loss charities Sands and Tommy's
OL,20,Fare calling on the Welsh government to
OL,21,Fensure bereaved parents are supported
OL,22,Fto contribute to the review of deaths.
OL,23,APub: 13-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
